usb: typec: ucsi: Read NOT_SUPPORTED partner PDOs as none

On the Dell XPS 14 DA14260, the PPM answers GET_PDOS for a charger's
sink PDOs with NOT_SUPPORTED rather than an empty list. The kernel logs
"UCSI_GET_PDOS failed (-95)", and ucsi_register_partner_pdos() returns
before typec_partner_set_usb_power_delivery(), so the charger's source
capabilities are registered but never linked to the partner: the
partner has no usb_power_delivery attribute.

A partner without PDOs for a role is what NOT_SUPPORTED means here, as
an empty answer does from other PPMs, so it's read as none and the
partner's other PDOs are still registered.

diff -ruN a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -877,6 +877,14 @@
 	command |= is_source(role) ? UCSI_GET_PDOS_SRC_PDOS : 0;
 	ret = ucsi_send_command(ucsi, command, pdos + offset,
 				num_pdos * sizeof(u32));
+	/*
+	 * Some PPMs answer NOT_SUPPORTED when the partner has no PDOs for a
+	 * role, such as a charger asked for its sink PDOs. It means the
+	 * partner has none, as an empty answer does, so its other PDOs are
+	 * still registered.
+	 */
+	if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP && is_partner)
+		return 0;
 	if (ret < 0 && ret != -ETIMEDOUT)
 		dev_err(ucsi->dev, "UCSI_GET_PDOS failed (%d)\n", ret);
 
